checklist:
- nginx configuration
- circuit breaker for endpoint
- rate limiter based on app, endpoint for service 1 reciever
- rate limit and concurrency on endpoint for consumer
- event driven using rabbitmq and for clearing outbox we will use loop
- idempotency handling at both service level
- metrics(p95 and counters), traces and logs using opentelemetry, prometheus and grafana
- follow lld patterns(like state machine) and solid principles
- normalized tables for service 1 and service 2

arch: 
- there will be two service here
- both service will be spring boot based
- both service will have their own db schema
- both service will communicate through rabbitmq
- wherever spring cache with redis provider is enough, we will use it, otherwise we will use direct redis
- projection table for fast reads and cqrs pattern will be followed
- dont overcomplicate things like pausing the ones which are already in queue, let them be processed and then pause the endpoint, same for disabling and expiring which applies only for new deliveries (so basically user can disable app, endpoint or event and it will not affect the ones which are already in queue -- re enable nothing happens)
- we will have three rabbitmq queues: main(only listen this), retry(proper delayed retry policy) and dlq(permanent or retry exhausted)
- cache lru and ttl, basically proper cache policies will be followed
- no hard delete, only soft delete

admin:
- manage apps, endpoints and receivers
- manage logs and telemetry

user: (through ui)
- register self, app, endpoints and receivers
- replay dlq messages
- can create a event through form, test endpoints using webhook --- ngrok/webhook.site
- delivery monitoring: view status of delivery and view metrics
- Generate, rotate, and revoke API keys, manage application settings like deactivate and rate limits, configure a webhook signing secret 

service1: "receiver service"
- m http thread(rest) for recieving event from customer and UI apis + n rabbitmq listener threads for status update from service2 + 1 loop thread for clearing outbox
- all ui api will be in this service (kind of bff but bff term is wrong since -- its tailor made for specific frontend)

service2: "delivery service"
- n rabbitmq listener threads for events from service1 and delivery to consumer + m http thread(grpc) for exposing status api for service1 + 1 loop thread for clearing outbox
- delivery will be done by this service and same thread working as listener and worker
- on completion of delivery, it will write to own db as well as raise event to service 1 for status update
- it exposes grpc api for service 1 to get updates of missed rabbitmq events, in case service 1 was down and missed the event
- sends delivery with idempotent key to consumer but consumer can choose to ignore it

