reasoning:
- first of all, below all points are for handling negative scenarios and not for happy path
- why people use callback -- because n services included can take time and cant wait for all, cant timeout and retry even though idempotent because thats bad for audit and loop causes latency + there are other events also like  refund, dispute, chargeback or reversal which requires callback
- why split in two services -- scaling and also because what if some endpoint is slow -- then receiver service impacted
- why rabbitmq -- because we dont want to again couple service a and service b(what if service b slow or down), due to same reason as why two service because endpoint can be down or slow
- outbox pattern because msg and db query in one transaction and for clearing as separate thread in service 1 because we dont want to block main thread and also because we can have multiple threads for sending events to rabbitmq -- we can argue here that loop brings latency 
- we can argue that in service 2 also have two threads for recieving and sending, but that just bring complexity and we can easily scale service 2 itself, so we can have n threads for listening and sending events to consumer
